WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:06.870
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:11.540
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.760
break up foreordination

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:27.640
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.390
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:32.980
No place

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:41.690
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.490
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:52.660
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.920
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.460
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.460
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:02.920
wake up your tough intention

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.840
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.090
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.730
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.310
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.780
break up foreordination

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.100
Yes.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.700
Yes. Understood. I'll do as you said.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.760
Thank you.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.080
Goodbye.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:39.660
Return
Goodbye.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.020
Return

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.660
Yeah... Is that so?

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.820
I'll make sure it gets approved.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.720
It'll be just fine...

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.890
By the way, what's the kid's name?

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.250
Ok, got it!

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.440
Alright, tell them what I said.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.750
Okay, thanks.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.560
Yeah, yeah...

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.850
So, you got in touch with them.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.830
Yeah. It seems like some big shot from HQ is coming,

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.720
and once I give them Argevollen, my job's done.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.810
Is that so?

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.070
They said we'd handle the
details upon arrival.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:26.840
That's great.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.040
I see.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.160
We're going to miss you.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.840
We were getting along so well, too...

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.440
You're right.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.780
I'm tired!

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.110
I'm hungry!

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.240
I can't wait to take a shower!

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.390
Yeah.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.840
When's the last time we took a bath?

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.340
I forget.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.620
My body feels so sticky.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.210
Hey, do I stink?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:20.700
Yeah.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.800
Seriously?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.740
Hold on!

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:23.840
What?

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.110
You stink, too!

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.620
Stop it!

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.280
Unit 8 is on standby until further notice.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.130
You're allowed to visit the surrounding suburbs,

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.480
but you need to make sure we can contact you.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:38.790
Any questions?

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.390
Okay, good work, everyone.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.570
Miss Hazaford.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:52.800
I've heard the details.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.240
A room's been prepared for you. Please wait there.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.990
Yes, thank you very much.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:58.950
See you later, Jamie!

00:03:58.950 --> 00:03:59.820
Yeah!

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.330
I'll take you there.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:23.870
You allowed vehicles, equipment, and
many other things to be destroyed.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.370
I did my best.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.750
That stuff's not free.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.770
Of course, you understand that.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.670
I'm well-aware.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.450
Was there no other way?

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.440
No.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.730
But...

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:41.010
The idea of dying from our own
equipment is a horrifying one.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:41.910
And...

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.560
And what?

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:47.560
I decided my priority was
the lives of my squad.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.300
In terms of cost?

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.150
No.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:55.650
And what of the other soldiers you
abandoned at the Gate of No Retreat?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.520
Enough of this.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:10.750
And that machine you brought in, what is it?

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:11.880
I don't know.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:16.040
The information we gathered from
the engineer we rescued is in the report.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.900
What a nuisance.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.690
We've decided

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.600
to leave its fate up to you.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:29.760
Understood.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.850
Is that true?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.790
Orders from the top.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.410
That's not official military equipment.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.800
Normally it would be impossible.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.070
What did you do?

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.030
I couldn't say.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.840
Enough. You're dismissed.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.640
Excuse me.

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:57.360
That's upsetting, even if it's an order.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.260
Colonel Izumi, maybe?

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.970
Brigadier General Cayenne
got permission, as well.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.250
I say! They were quick on the draw.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:09.190
Colonel Izumi is the one who gave him a commando unit, too.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.310
Even if they went to officer school together,

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.980
isn't he being a little too nice to him?

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:16.480
Yes, but there's nothing we can do about it.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:22.050
A man who was once on the fast track is now stuck out here.

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:25.440
As a friend he has to help him, I suppose.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.000
A beautiful friendship?

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.520
I don't know.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.440
We must rebuild the northwestern front forces and counterattack!

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.010
If we gather all our forces together,
we can wipe them out—

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.040
What forces, exactly?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.420
What?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.550
We took heavy losses!

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.720
And since we retreated without
launching any kind of counterattack,

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.390
the soldiers' morale is low!

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.940
Did you send a request for reinforcements to HQ?

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.010
Nobody has any reinforcements to send.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.640
So we admit defeat?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.100
We accept reality!

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.990
Okay.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.540
See you later.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.400
Where are you going, Lorenz?

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.870
I was gonna ask Jamie out to lunch.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.650
We finally got leave!

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.790
You should do what you want, too.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.560
R&R is important!

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.770
I hear you.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.880
Bye.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.590
Hey, Okui! Wait!

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:00.640
Okui! Calm down! Okay?

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.880
You're such a pain.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.170
Hey there.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:04.940
Hey.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:06.510
Wait, Okui!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:07.740
Shut up!

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.750
Okui?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.760
Stop it!

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:32.780
Don't try to stop me!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.250
Just calm down, okay?

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.250
Let's get some food!
You're mad because you're hungry.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.120
Okay? Okay?

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.750
It's not okay, damn it!

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.470
What do you think is going to happen now?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:51.400
Nothing, the way things are looking.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.960
Are we going to strike back?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.430
Probably not.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.430
But there are rumors that a large part of our forces has been wiped out.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.600
I'm amazed we made it back.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.610
Yeah.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.160
We're lucky just to be alive.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.360
Okay, I'm heading out.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.030
Okay.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.490
Jamie?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.170
Huh?

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:28.070
It's all caught up to you, finally.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.320
Here.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.680
Well done.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:44.170
Your selfishness put your entire unit at risk!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.110
Right...

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:48.250
I don't want to die for the likes of you!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.450
I'm sorry.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.130
The captain's orders are absolute.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:54.270
Don't go running off on your own!

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.640
Isn't that enough?

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.100
You feel better?

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:03.600
Well, I don't know if what you did was wrong.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.460
Tanita!

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:08.720
At the end of the day, you did manage to save her.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:13.840
I don't know what I would've done if I were in your shoes.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.360
I think I'd've left her to die.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:16.940
Seriously? That's cold!

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.470
Nah, if it's a girl, I'll save her.

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:26.320
But seriously, what Okui said is true, too.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.560
You're right.

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:32.840
Look out.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.280
At this rate, you won't last long.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.140
Well, reflect on that a little.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.410
That's right.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.900
Yeah.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.390
And apologize to the captain, too.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.570
It's been eight years since then.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.490
How's the enemy?

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.640
We sealed the Gate of No Retreat.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.030
That has to have slowed them down.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.040
It's only a matter of time, though.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:24.790
Would you turn back?

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:30.000
I'm going to back asking a lot of you.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.790
That's fine.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.800
That makes it easier to not think about it.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:52.950
I hate it, even if it happens every time.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:54.390
It's not your fault.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:57.240
There had to have been another way.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:11:59.990
I'm sorry.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.030
I'm just complaining.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:07.230
Are you sure about that machine?

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:10.000
I'd like to think I did what you asked.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:14.200
I did everything I could to look into it,

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.880
but I couldn't find anything.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.000
Nothing?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.010
Yeah.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.660
Normally if you made something like that,
there would at least be rumors.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.540
Whatever information controls
they're using must be amazing.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:31.730
The Kivernas Manufacturing Company, was it?

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.150
They're not normal.

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:45.950
Sorry, but I'll be going.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.980
The man supposedly in charge
of that thing has appeared.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:03.760
I'm honored to meet you, Lt. Samonji.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:07.530
May I call you Mr. Suguro?

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:09.020
Go ahead.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.870
This has been such a bother.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:15.020
The whole company is in an uproar.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.410
So what can I do for you?

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.460
Let me be brief...

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.620
I'm sure you've heard, but...

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.670
We'll take good care of it.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.640
That's a prototype. We can't lose it.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.550
A prototype? It moved extremely well.

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:32.790
Of course it did.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.970
The fate of our company depends on it.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:37.380
I see.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.950
It worked without issue, then?

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:40.760
Yes.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.150
I'm sure our employee has
already told you this,

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:47.020
but there's a testing ground near that area.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.490
If we'd known this was going to happen,

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:52.350
we would've tried to get it somewhere safe.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.270
I see.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.970
But the plan got messed up.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.780
It truly is a bother.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.220
I look forward to working with you.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:07.320
Oh, and about that employee of ours...

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.280
Are you sure about this, Lieutenant?

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.200
She's an engineer, but she's still wet behind the ears.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.880
Do we have the right to refuse?

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.520
This way.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:36.020
I'll be on my way, then.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.510
So you're the girl?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.830
Um, may I help you?

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.330
I'm Suguro, from company HQ.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.930
I'm Jamie Hazaford! Nice to meet you!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.930
Nice to meet you. Sounds like you've had a rough time.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.010
Not at all, you've had it worse!

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:02.000
B-But I'm sorry this happened...

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.740
No, you did well to bring it back intact.

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:07.050
I thank you.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.890
Not at all, thank <i>you</i>!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.100
So, what's the pilot's name?

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.680
What are you doing?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.780
Um...

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:24.980
I didn't realize...

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:31.100
When I disobeyed your orders,
I put the whole unit in danger.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.660
Is that what you came here to say?

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.120
No, um...

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.490
I disobeyed an order!

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:41.380
But I haven't been punished!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.620
And you want to be punished?

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:47.140
No, well...

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.400
Private Susumu.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.650
Yes, sir.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:53.740
Normally, you'd stand in front
of a military tribunal.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:55.770
Yes, sir...

00:15:55.770 --> 00:16:00.500
To be honest, I was
considering having you shot.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.780
Yes, sir...

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.550
The person who receives the
orders carries them out.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.290
And who takes responsibility for that?

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.180
The man who gave the order.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.290
Yes.

00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:18.180
Personal feelings have no role in it.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:19.490
For either of us.

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.490
Yes, sir.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:22.500
Otherwise, we can't do our jobs.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:38.980
But... How do you really feel?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.560
How do I feel?

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.190
About what you did.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.490
I'm the same as you.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.960
I see.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:57.530
Yes. But there was a time when it wouldn't work.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:58.910
I'm sure.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.690
This thing is intended to be booted and operated by the same person.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:07.880
I never imagined it could function with two people.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.920
Um... can you fix it?

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.670
To be honest, we can't restore it.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.890
I-I see...

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:18.410
Problematic indeed!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:20.750
Oh, thank you.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.620
E-Excuse me.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:26.440
You said you wanted to go back to your old department?

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:28.460
Th-That's right!

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.400
I see.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.830
Um... is there an issue?

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:38.730
What do you think?

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.330
Could you take responsibility?

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:43.510
Am I fired? You can't do that—

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:45.370
No, no.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:48.340
You've been given official instructions from HQ.

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:52.220
Certainly, as a soldier, and as a

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:56.850
as a subordinate, what you did was wrong.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:01.730
But that doesn't mean I think what you did was wrong.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.740
I think that an individual's feelings may sometimes be what saves an organization.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.930
I'll never tell you to destroy your feelings.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:24.640
I think it's okay for an army, an organization, to be that way.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.510
Argevollen...

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:37.220
You're going to stay with this.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.210
It's in your keeping.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:44.480
Make good use of the power you've been given.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.990
I'm expecting great things.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.240
Right!

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.400
I can't! That's impossible!

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:02.540
I've already told the military.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.700
Then get someone else!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.600
You've already become the activation key.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.960
No one but you can activate it.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.590
If it's a program, can't you just reset it?

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.610
It's not that easy.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:17.040
B-But it's impossible! I can't!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:19.290
If you work hard, we'll take care of you.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:21.720
I know! You'll get a bonus.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.310
The company will treat it as an extended company trip.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.940
No! No! I can't!

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:29.770
Really?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:30.360
I can't.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:33.820
Well, this is a problem...

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.630
Which means you're fired.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.620
At best.

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.160
Do you understand?

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.130
You're telling me you'll destroy the company.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.510
Do you know how much this machine costs?

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:53.990
If you won't do it...

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:58.640
Well, I don't suppose we'd demand compensation...

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.660
Well actually, knowing our company...

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:12.490
Well, give it some thought.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:39.970
Why?

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:03.870
It's him...

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:32.450
I'm home, Sis.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.150
I just got back.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.540
I'm going to find them.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:45.440
I'm going to find the person who killed you.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:47.910
And then...

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:41.240
Surprise Attack
